@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# `hush script-scan`: local script and project scanner (added after 2.1.0)
+
+Read-only, offline, no model needed. It reads files as text and applies fixed rules. It never executes, imports, extracts or fetches anything, never contacts a URL it finds, and skips symbolic links. It writes a file only when you pass `--report` (atomic, refuses to overwrite without `--overwrite`).
+
+## Usage
+```
+hush script-scan PATH [--json] [--report OUT [--overwrite]] [--baseline SHA256SUMS] [--allow-host HOST]... [--fail-on low|medium|high|critical]
+```
+`PATH` is a file or a folder (up to 5,000 files, 8 levels deep, 5 MiB per file; larger files are hashed, not scanned). `--fail-on` makes the exit code 3 when a finding at or above that level exists, for use in CI. `--baseline` takes a `sha256sum`-style file and reports modified, new and missing files. `--allow-host` silences URLs to that host and its subdomains.
+
+## What it reads
+| Kind | Detected by | Checked for |
+|---|---|---|
+| Python | `.py .pyw .pyi`, shebang | subprocess / os.system / popen / exec, eval, `__import__`, pickle/marshal, ctypes, socket / urllib / http / requests / ftplib / smtplib / telnetlib / websocket / paramiko, delete and write-mode `open()`, decode-then-execute |
+| Lua, EEL | `.lua .eel` | os.execute, io.popen, load / loadstring / dofile / loadfile, package.loadlib / cpath, luasocket, delete / rename / write-mode `io.open` |
+| REAPER scripts (Lua/EEL/Python) | same | `ExecProcess` (incl. Python `RPR_ExecProcess`), SWS `CF_ShellExecute`, `AddRemoveReaScript`, persistent `SetExtState(..., true)`, `js_ReaScriptAPI` memory calls, `reaper.defer` loops, `__startup.*` file names |
+| JSFX | `.jsfx`, `desc:` header | file access |
+| REAPER project / actions | `.RPP`, `reaper-kb.ini` | plugin inventory (`<VST`, `<CLAP`, `<JS`, `<AU`), media paths outside the project, plugin-state blobs counted (not analyzed), registered scripts and custom actions |
+| Shell, batch, PowerShell | `.sh .bash .bat .cmd .ps1`, Makefile, Dockerfile | curl / wget, pipe into sh, `/dev/tcp`, `nc -e`, rm -rf, Invoke-Expression / iex, `-EncodedCommand`, DownloadString / DownloadFile, certutil, bitsadmin, reg add, schtasks |
+| JavaScript, C/C++ | `.js .mjs .ts`, `.c .cpp .h ...` | child_process, eval, fetch / XHR / WebSocket; system, popen, exec*, dlopen, LoadLibrary, socket |
+| Any text or config | everything else | URLs (cleartext, IP literals, `.onion`), secrets by kind (values redacted), long base64 / hex blobs, `\x` escape floods, very long lines, persistence keywords (cron, systemd, launchd, Run key, authorized_keys) |
+| Binaries, archives | magic bytes | hashed and listed only; native plugin files (`.vst3 .clap .dll .so .dylib ...`) are inventoried as "not analyzed"; archives are not opened |
+UTF-16 files with a byte-order mark are read as their ASCII subset.
+
+## Limits (read these)
+- Pattern matching: expect false positives (a legitimate `os.system` call) and false negatives. Heavy obfuscation, string building and indirection defeat it.
+- Comments and Python docstrings are skipped for code rules by a simple parser, not a full language parser.
+- No data-flow analysis. It cannot tell whether a command line is constant or attacker-controlled.
+- Compiled code and archives are never analyzed. Use the hashes and your plugin allowlist.
+- REAPER API names come from my knowledge of ReaScript; check them against your REAPER version.
+- Output severities and confidence numbers are rule defaults, not measured probabilities.
+
+Self-scan note: scanning HUSH's own tree reports High findings in `src/script_scan.cpp`, `tests/script_scan_tests.cpp` and `SCRIPT_SCAN_NOTES.md` (they contain the patterns as data), in the smoke test's `rm -rf` cleanup, and in the `optional/` installers (genuine). All were reviewed; none is unexpected. Treat scans of security documents and rule tables the same way.
+
+## Evidence
+`tests/script_scan_tests.cpp` (55 checks), 13 CLI steps in `scripts/smoke_test.sh`; outputs in `evidence/script_scan/`.
